<h2>Questions from Blaine property owners</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>What’s the difference between tornado and straight-line wind for insurance purposes?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>For most homeowner policies, both fall under windstorm coverage. The difference matters more for how damage is documented than whether it is covered.</p></div></details><details><summary>Can I invoke appraisal if my insurer hasn’t finished the claim yet?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Appraisal is usually available once there is a disagreement over the amount. Many policies also set deadlines for lawsuits, so don’t wait too long. Read your policy or ask a lawyer about timing.</p></div></details></div>
